# 8. MAP VISUAL STYLE

The map itself should be visually clean.

Prefer:

* light map
* muted roads
* subtle geographic colors
* readable city names
* restrained map labels

Do NOT use:

* dark futuristic map
* neon roads
* glowing terrain
* sci-fi map
* excessive satellite effects

The map should allow the selected location marker to stand out.

---

# 9. LOCATION PIN

Use a fixed/clear selection marker.

Preferred interaction:

The user moves the map underneath the marker.

The marker remains visually centered.

Example:

```
         📍
          |
   ┌──────────────┐
   │     MAP      │
   │              │
   │              │
   └──────────────┘
```

As the user moves the map:

latitude and longitude update.

The selected location should therefore correspond to the center of the map.

This is similar to the practical map-selection pattern used by delivery applications.

